{
    "background_story": "Snookums was a curious and contemplative cat who spent most of her days lounging in the sun-drenched study of her owner, a philosophy professor. As the professor pored over the works of Henri Bergson, Snookums would sit by her side, listening intently to the musings on time and consciousness. She seemed to grasp the concept of dur\u00e9e, Bergson's notion of time as a fluid, lived experience, and would often pause mid-pounce to savor the moment. Snookums' owner believed that the cat's ability to live in the present was a manifestation of Bergson's philosophy, and would often remark that Snookums was the embodiment of \u00e9lan vital, the vital energy that drives all living beings. As the professor worked, Snookums would provide a soothing presence, reminding her of the importance of living in the present moment.",
